# .platform/ is read-only

In a Yes Human pack, `.platform/` is a fresh clone of the platform made by `.cursor/install.sh`. It is not part of this repo and is replaced on every install.

- Do not commit, push, or open PRs from `.platform/`.
- The pack's `.cursor/*` files are managed by Yes Human too. If install fails, do not rewrite them; file an `agent-feedback` issue on the pack (see its `AGENTS.md`) and stop.
- Change this pack (config, theme, seeds, `plugin/`) when the platform's extension points allow it.
- When a request needs a platform change, you may prototype in `.platform/` to prove it, then file a `platform-request` issue on this pack with the diff. See the `yh-platform-request` skill.
